<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="44092" href="schedule/2018/fall/ECE/586/44092.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2018" href="schedule/2018.xml">2018</calendarYear><term id="120188" href="schedule/2018/fall.xml">Fall 2018</term><subject id="ECE" href="schedule/2018/fall/ECE.xml">Electrical and Computer Engineering</subject><course id="586" href="schedule/2018/fall/ECE/586.xml">Topics in Decision and Control</course></parents><sectionNumber>DL </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Hybrid Systems and Control</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Switched/hybrid systems are dynamical systems that combine continuous dynamics and discrete events. Such systems are of theoretical interest and important in many applications, and they have attracted considerable attention in the recent control literature. This advanced graduate-level course will introduce the students to recent research results on analysis and design of switched and hybrid systems. Prerequisite: ECE 515.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2018-08-27Z</startDate><endDate>2018-12-12Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>4070</roomNumber><buildingName>Electrical &amp; Computer Eng Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Liberzon" firstName="D">Liberzon, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>